### customer-account — requisições de exemplo (REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP Client)
### Pré-requisito: docker compose up -d --build

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@keycloak = http://localhost:8180/realms/customer-account/protocol/openid-connect/token

### 1) Token do Tenant A (client credentials)
# @name tokenA
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=tenant-app-a&client_secret=tenant-app-a-dev-secret

### 2) Token do Tenant B
# @name tokenB
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=tenant-app-b&client_secret=tenant-app-b-dev-secret

### 3) Cadastrar cliente (Tenant A)
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cpf": "529.982.247-25",
  "personalData": {
    "fullName": "Maria da Silva Souza",
    "socialName": null,
    "birthDate": "1990-05-20",
    "motherName": "Ana da Silva",
    "maritalStatus": "MARRIED",
    "nationality": "BR"
  },
  "email": "maria.souza@example.com",
  "mobilePhone": "(11) 91234-5678",
  "address": {
    "zipCode": "01310-100",
    "street": "Avenida Paulista",
    "number": "1000",
    "complement": "Apto 101",
    "district": "Bela Vista",
    "city": "São Paulo",
    "state": "SP"
  }
}

### 4) Consultar (Tenant A) — leitura do read model (pode levar alguns ms após o cadastro)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/{{register.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA.response.body.access_token}}

### 5) Buscar por CPF (CPF no corpo)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/search
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "cpf": "52998224725" }

### 6) Isolamento: Tenant B não enxerga o cliente do Tenant A (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/{{register.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenB.response.body.access_token}}

### 7) Alterar e-mail
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/{{register.response.body.id}}/email
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "maria.nova@example.com" }

### 8) Alterar endereço
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/{{register.response.body.id}}/address
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "zipCode": "20040-020",
  "street": "Avenida Rio Branco",
  "number": "1",
  "district": "Centro",
  "city": "Rio de Janeiro",
  "state": "RJ"
}

### 9) Eliminar dados (LGPD) — crypto-shredding
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/{{register.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA.response.body.access_token}}

### ===================== Validações (fase 2) =====================

### 10) Token do administrador do Tenant A (DEV: password grant; produção = authorization code + PKCE + MFA)
# @name adminA
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=tenant-app-a-admin&username=admin.tenant-a&password=dev&scope=openid

### 11) Provedores disponíveis na plataforma
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tenant/verification-providers
Authorization: Bearer {{adminA.response.body.access_token}}

### 12) Admin define o provedor de FACE_MATCH com contingência (vale na próxima validação)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tenant/verification-policy/rules/FACE_MATCH
Authorization: Bearer {{adminA.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "primaryProvider": "simulated-unavailable",
  "fallbackProvider": "simulated-approve",
  "minimumScore": 70,
  "onInconclusive": "MANUAL_REVIEW",
  "enabled": true,
  "reason": "Contrato inicial"
}

### 13) Política vigente e histórico de alterações
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tenant/verification-policy/history
Authorization: Bearer {{adminA.response.body.access_token}}

### 14) Tenant solicita validação (cadastre um cliente antes, passo 3)
# @name verification
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/verifications
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": "{{register.response.body.id}}", "type": "FACE_MATCH" }

### 15) Resultado padronizado (read model)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/verifications/{{verification.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA.response.body.access_token}}

### 16) Falhas de provedores registradas para o tenant
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tenant/verification-incidents?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{adminA.response.body.access_token}}

### ===================== OTP e webhook (fase 2b) =====================

### 17) Admin cadastra o webhook (guarde o "secret": aparece só agora). Receptor de teste: qualquer servidor na máquina
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tenant/webhook
Authorization: Bearer {{adminA.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "url": "http://host.docker.internal:9999/hooks/customer-account" }

### 18) Admin define OTP próprio para posse de e-mail
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tenant/verification-policy/rules/EMAIL_OWNERSHIP
Authorization: Bearer {{adminA.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "primaryProvider": "own-email-otp",
  "onInconclusive": "REJECT",
  "enabled": true,
  "reason": "OTP por e-mail"
}

### 19) Tenant inicia a validação: status AWAITING_CONFIRMATION (código no Mailpit: http://localhost:8025)
# @name otp
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/verifications
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": "{{register.response.body.id}}", "type": "EMAIL_OWNERSHIP" }

### 20) Tenant envia o código digitado pelo titular
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/verifications/{{otp.response.body.id}}/confirmation
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "123456" }

### 21) Entregas do webhook (status, tentativas, último erro)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tenant/webhook/deliveries
Authorization: Bearer {{adminA.response.body.access_token}}

### ===================== Identidade hospedada (fase 3a) =====================

### 22) Admin define Legitimuz/Netrin (simulated-hosted para desenvolvimento) e regras do resultado
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tenant/verification-policy/rules/IDENTITY
Authorization: Bearer {{adminA.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "primaryProvider": "simulated-hosted",
  "fallbackProvider": null,
  "minimumScore": 70,
  "onInconclusive": "MANUAL_REVIEW",
  "enabled": true,
  "reason": "Teste de identidade hospedada",
  "scoreBelowAction": "MANUAL_REVIEW",
  "fraudReasonCodes": ["DOCUMENT_TAMPERED"],
  "manualReviewReasonCodes": ["NEEDS_REVIEW"],
  "onProviderError": "ERROR",
  "validityDays": 90,
  "allowedReturnUrlPrefixes": ["https://front.example/app"]
}

### 23) Tenant solicita o link. Abra link.url no navegador para escolher o resultado de teste
# @name identity
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/verifications
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": "{{register.response.body.id}}", "type": "IDENTITY", "returnUrl": "https://front.example/app/return" }

### 24) Pedir novamente retorna 200 + reused=true enquanto o link estiver ativo
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/verifications
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": "{{register.response.body.id}}", "type": "IDENTITY" }

### 25) Status atual (ou use GET /api/v1/verifications/{{identity.response.body.id}} para detalhes)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/{{register.response.body.id}}/verification-status?type=IDENTITY
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA.response.body.access_token}}
